---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import DifferentialCryptanalysisLogo from '../assets/images/logos/DifferentialCryptanalysisLogo.svg';
import ProjectHeader from './ProjectHeader.astro';
---
<div>
  <ProjectHeader title="Differential Cryptanalysis" subtitle="Master’s project" logo={DifferentialCryptanalysisLogo} custommargin="5px" link="https://maticstric.github.io/differential-cryptanalysis-tutorial/" />
  <p>
    Differential cryptanalysis is a subtle, beautiful, and powerful method of breaking some of the world’s strongest ciphers.
    Despite its significance, educational resources on the subject are scarce, and those that do exist can be difficult to follow, particularly for readers new to cryptography.
    This tutorial, developed as my Master’s project, aims to bridge that gap by introducing differential cryptanalysis to beginners through an interactive, self-contained webpage that requires no prior knowledge of the subject.
  </p>
  <p>
    Alongside the tutorial, I developed a small HTML component library in C and three Python implementations of differential cryptanalysis.
    The first demonstrates the technique against a simple toy cipher.
    The second applies it to a more complex substitution-permutation network (SPN) cipher, prioritizing readability over efficiency.
    The third provides a more sophisticated implementation, demonstrating a practical approach to attacking generic SPN ciphers.
  </p>
</div>